WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.526
Welcome to Module 6 Joining Data in PostgreSQL Up to
this point

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:10.079
we have often worked with one table at a time Real
analytical

00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:16.648
questions usually require information that is stored
across several related tables In

00:00:16.674 --> 00:00:20.201
this module the important question is not simply how
do I write

00:00:20.227 --> 00:00:24.572
a JOIN The more important question is what should
one output row

00:00:24.585 --> 00:00:28.558
represent which rows must remain even when no match
exists and can

00:00:28.572 --> 00:00:33.638
either side match more than once We will work with
INNER LEFT

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:38.233
RIGHT and FULL OUTER joins We will also compare ON
and WHERE

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:42.075
use self joins and cross joins and spend extra time
on cardinality

00:00:42.101 --> 00:00:45.720
because row multiplication is one of the most common
causes of incorrect

00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:51.375
analytical results As you work through the examples
run the SQL

00:00:51.401 --> 00:00:55.956
directly in the browser On code slides you can also
use Copy

00:00:55.983 --> 00:01:00.470
and paste the same query into the pgAdmin Query Tool
The goal

00:01:00.496 --> 00:01:04.338
is to learn a repeatable reasoning process not only
join syntax
